 "notes": [
  "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
  "The parts list says 100 ohm resistors but the schematic label says 10k ohm; I used 100 ohm from the parts list.",
  "Each speaker's red lead goes to the breadboard in the same column as one resistor leg. The resistor spans the centre gap, and its other end shares a column with that channel's jumper wire. So each Arduino pin (8, 7, 6) drives one speaker through its own resistor.",
  "The three speaker black leads go to the top ground rail, and a black wire joins that rail to Arduino GND.",
  "I used the catalogue's naming: bank 'b' is rows f-j, which is the upper half in the image. The image's top rail row nearest the black line is 'tn'.",
  "The exact rail hole numbers (tn.1, tn.6, tn.14, tn.22) are read off the image and are approximate. All holes on the rail are one strip, so the electrical result is the same.",
  "The speakers are non-polarised and their two leads are symmetric. Port 1 is the red lead and port 2 is the black lead."
 ],
